# Copy to environment-owned restricted storage, not a research/cache directory.
# Literal image/platform pins and serving options are owned by the release manifest.
MEMORYOS_INFERENCE_ASSETS_ROOT=/var/lib/memoryos-inference/assets
MEMORYOS_INFERENCE_CACHE_ROOT=/var/cache/memoryos-inference
MEMORYOS_INFERENCE_CONTROL_DIR=/var/lib/memoryos-inference/control
MEMORYOS_INFERENCE_API_KEY_FILE=/etc/memoryos/secrets/inference-api-key
MEMORYOS_INFERENCE_CLIENT_NETWORK=memoryos-inference-client
MEMORYOS_INFERENCE_BACKEND_NETWORK=memoryos-inference-backend

# Linux preconditions, performed by the authorized environment operator:
# - Assets root: operator-owned 0755, no symlink component; provision.py publishes
#   revision children0555 and exact files0444. Never delete old assets/caches here.
# - Cache root: UID/GID1654, mode0700, separate from assets; launcher creates private
#   cache children. Existing cache children must retain UID1654 and mode0700.
# - Control directory: root/operator-owned0755; maintenance marker0644 blocks new
#   generations503 while active streams drain. Directory remains mounted, so marker
#   create/remove is visible without recreating gateway. Not an admission queue.
# - Key: regular nonsymlink file UID/GID1654 mode0400, exactly64 lowercase hex
#   characters plus at most one final LF. No key values in env/argv/logs.
# - Engine/gateway run UID/GID1654, readonly rootfs, dropped capabilities.
#   Provisioning is an operator HTTPS command; neither serving network has egress.
# - Check physical AND Docker/cache disk free space and actual available memory
#   against manifest.hostRequirements before launch; an allocation is not a quota.
# - Only API/gateway join client; only gateway/engine/authorized Prometheus join
#   backend. Docker aliases require the same accepted private Docker host.
# - For isolated qualification choose distinct roots/network names and -p; keep
#   research resources/credentials untouched. No product port is host-published.
#
# Operator commands (run from the repository/release root; never source this file):
# python3 infrastructure/inference/managed/provision.py --manifest infrastructure/inference/managed/manifest.json --assets-root /var/lib/memoryos-inference/assets
# python3 infrastructure/inference/managed/provision.py --manifest infrastructure/inference/managed/manifest.json --assets-root /var/lib/memoryos-inference/assets --verify-only
# docker compose --env-file /etc/memoryos/inference.env -f infrastructure/deployment/compose.inference.yaml up -d --wait --wait-timeout 600
# docker compose --env-file /etc/memoryos/inference.env -f infrastructure/deployment/compose.inference.yaml exec -T vllm /opt/venv/bin/python3 /opt/memoryos-inference/probe.py --manifest /opt/memoryos-inference/manifest.json --key-file /run/secrets/inference_api_key --base-url http://inference-gateway:8080 --mode ready
# The same probe with --mode generation exercises real SSE; --mode idle requires
# --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8000 and observes native running/waiting/counter quiet8s.
# Stop only after the Ops-owned maintenance/drain procedure; rotation must recreate
# BOTH containers (file bind mounts and in-process credentials do not hot-reload).
# Application: add -f infrastructure/deployment/compose.inference.application.yaml
# to normal application Compose invocation. Keep hosted bootstrap/default unchanged;
# model managers configure http://inference-gateway:8080/v1 via normal encrypted BYOK.
